It is well-documented that the $\chi^2=\alpha R + \beta R^2$ action plays a crucial role in both cosmology and black hole physics. In cosmology, it gives rise to an effective cosmological constant. In the context of black holes, it helps construct regular solutions free of singularities. This section reviews these two bodies of work.

